Q. On all Coors beer cans there is a note that states that all aluminum beer cans may be recycled. I feel that this is
to cut down on garbage, but where in El Paso can a person send these beer cans or have them picked up?—H.E.
A. Andrew Cohen, public relations and sales manager for Dickshire Coors, said that Dickshire accepts Coors cans and
any aluminum beer cans from 12 to 3 p.m. Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday at the company, 203 N. Chelsea, and pays 10 cents per pound. Last week Cohen said, Dickshire took in 30,000 pounds of cans,
and during the year has taken in more than 300,000 pounds, representing 6,900,000 cans which Dickshire has helped to keep off the roads and highways. After
crushing and baling in El Paso, the cans are sent to the Coors brewery in Denver for recycling, he said.

